From 87dda0cced03ebdd5d921a5fc8c8a7bdc2bc323b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Balister <philip@balister.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:58:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test: name the Studio sinks' update interval and input count
 as declared

The Studio compatibility graphs set poll_ms on StudioSeriesSink and
StudioWaterfallSink and channels on StudioSeriesSink. Neither sink
declares them: gr4-studio renamed poll_ms to update_ms, and the series
sink counts its inputs in n_inputs. The graph loader used to move such
a key into the block's meta_information, so the sinks ran at their
defaults. gnuradio4-core 7f43a66 makes the loader refuse it, and the
four Studio compatibility tests fail to prepare their session:

  block 'series0' of type 'gr::studio::StudioSeriesSink<float32>'
  declares no setting named 'poll_ms'; the nearest are 'update_ms', ...

Name them update_ms and n_inputs.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Philip Balister <philip@balister.org>
---
 test/gr4_runtime_manager_test.cpp | 6 +++---
 test/http_api_test.cpp            | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/test/gr4_runtime_manager_test.cpp b/test/gr4_runtime_manager_test.cpp
index ae67bff..89e6e54 100644
--- a/test/gr4_runtime_manager_test.cpp
+++ b/test/gr4_runtime_manager_test.cpp
@@ -120,9 +120,9 @@ std::string compatibility_studio_http_series_graph_yaml() {
       stream:
         transport: "http_poll"
         payload_format: "series-window-json-v1"
-      poll_ms: 250
+      update_ms: 250
       window_size: 64
-      channels: 1
+      n_inputs: 1
 connections:
   - ["src0", "out", "series0", "in#0"]
 )";
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@ std::string compatibility_studio_http_waterfall_graph_yaml() {
       stream:
         transport: "http_poll"
         payload_format: "waterfall-spectrum-json-v1"
-      poll_ms: 250
+      update_ms: 250
       fft_size: 32
       sample_rate: 1000.0
       time_span: 0.256
diff --git a/test/http_api_test.cpp b/test/http_api_test.cpp
index c403fbf..88e7c1f 100644
--- a/test/http_api_test.cpp
+++ b/test/http_api_test.cpp
@@ -289,9 +289,9 @@ std::string compatibility_studio_http_poll_graph() {
       stream:
         transport: "http_poll"
         payload_format: "series-window-json-v1"
-      poll_ms: 250
+      update_ms: 250
       window_size: 64
-      channels: 1
+      n_inputs: 1
 connections:
   - ["src0", "out", "series0", "in#0"]
 )";
